Glaxosmithkline Intellectual Property (No. 3) Limited; Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited; Amgen Inc.; Novartis Pharma AG; Madrigal Pharmaceuticals, Inc.; and Sarepta Therapeutics, Inc. Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Pasadena, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Christopher R. Anzalone Ph.D. | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $424K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 63%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $64K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.1B market cap on $451M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years and +122% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -72% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $284M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u201